      "Integration by parts with $u=x^2$, $v'=\\mathrm{e}^x$: $u'=2x$, $v=\\mathrm{e}^x$, so $\\int x^2\\mathrm{e}^x\\,dx=x^2\\mathrm{e}^x-\\int 2x\\,\\mathrm{e}^x\\,dx$.",
